course: dictionary
lesson: 15761
title: Words that cause trouble
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A troublesome thing causes trouble, worry or difficulty. It can be a person, an animal, a problem or a thing. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The cough was troublesome, and it kept Sam awake all night.» A cough that keeps you awake is causing trouble, so troublesome means causing trouble or difficulty.
explain: Troublesome can also describe a person. «Toad was a troublesome friend, always starting new crazes that worried Badger, Rat and Mole.» The clue is worried: Toad's crazes gave his friends worry, so he was annoying and hard to deal with.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Put "causing trouble" in place of troublesome: "The old gate is causing trouble: it sticks every time you open it." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Troublesome is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a troublesome cough, a troublesome knee.
fact: Troublesome means causing trouble, worry or difficulty. It can also mean annoying or hard to deal with.
fact: «Troublesome» can describe people, animals, problems and things.
fact: Its other forms are more troublesome and most troublesome: «The stain was more troublesome than the spill.»
fact: «Trouble» is the noun, meaning a problem or a bother. «Troublesome» is the describing word made from it.
exercise: «The cough was troublesome, and it kept Sam awake all night.» What does troublesome mean? | Very quiet | Pleasant and calming | Bright and shiny | *Causing trouble or difficulty
exercise: Find and copy the describing word: «My knee is troublesome when it rains.» | rains | knee | when | *troublesome
exercise: A maths question that is hard to solve can be called a troublesome question. What is a troublesome question? | *A hard question that causes difficulty | A very short question | A question with a picture | A question about trouble
test: «The gate is troublesome: it sticks every time you open it.» What does troublesome mean here? | Shiny and new | Quick to open | Cheap | *Causing difficulty
test: Which word means causing trouble or worry? | Gentle | *Troublesome | Calm | Pleasant
exam: «My neighbour's barking dog is so troublesome that Mr Patel complained to the council.» What does troublesome mean here? | *Annoying and hard to deal with | Friendly | Tiny | Silent
